{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2ekpuglckix4x26klwfiaorz3qcol6nneacid6lojabazsq2uthq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single 647-line C file: a `cute_c2`-derived 2D collision library (vector math, GJK distance solver with a simplex cache, and circle/AABB/capsule intersection tests) plus one function `capsule()` — the only thing declared in `include/lib.h`. There are **no** namespace-renaming macros, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Completion gate: symbol parity\n\nBuilt the C library with CMake and diffed `nm -D` against my Rust `.so`:\n\n```\nC exports: 38   Rust exports: 38   diff: EMPTY (no missing, no extra)\n```\n\nAll 38: `c22 c23 c2AABBtoAABB c2AABBtoCapsule c2Add c2BBVerts c2CCW90 c2CapsuletoCapsule c2CircletoAABB c2CircletoCapsule c2CircletoCircle c2Clampv c2Collided c2D c2Det2 c2Div c2Dot c2GJK c2GJKSimplexMetric c2L c2Len c2MakeProxy c2Maxv c2Minv c2Mulrv c2MulrvT c2Mulvs c2Mulxv c2Neg c2Norm c2RotIdentity c2Skew c2Sub c2Support c2V c2Witness c2xIdentity capsule`\n\n## Bit-exactness verification\n\nI wrote a differential harness that `dlopen`s **both** libraries, calls every exported symbol with identical inputs, and `memcmp`s results (float bits, out-params, and mutated `c2Simplex`/`c2GJKCache`/`c2Proxy` state):\n\n| Configuration | Checks | Failures |\n|---|---|---|\n| finite inputs, all 38 symbols | 21,300,002 | 0 |\n| inf/NaN/denormal/FLT_MAX inputs | 21,300,002 | 0 |\n| 50 % NaN density, 12 distinct payloads incl. sNaN & both signs | 21,300,002 | 0 |\n| GJK cache path (in-contract indices) | 21,300,002 | 0 |\n| realistic cache reuse across successive calls | 1,600,000 | 0 |\n| `capsule()` + booleans, fully random 32-bit patterns | 10,000,000 | 0 |\n\nTo reach exactness on non-finite inputs I had to reproduce **x86 SSE NaN propagation**: `mulss/addss/subss/divss` let the *destination* operand win, quiet an sNaN in place, and yield the indefinite QNaN `0xFFC00000` for invalid ops on non-NaN operands. GCC's `-O0` register allocation picks a non-obvious destination at several sites (e.g. `c2Dot` multiplies `a.x*b.x` with `a.x` as destination but `a.y*b.y` with `b.y` as destination). I disassembled every function, recorded the destination at each site, and encoded it via small `mul_ss/add_ss/sub_ss/div_ss` helpers — which are exact no-ops for non-NaN operands.\n\n## Fidelity details preserved (not \"fixed\")\n\n- `c2GJKSimplexMetric`'s `default:` falling through into `case 1:`; `c2D`/`c2L`'s merged `case 3`/`default`.\n- `c2MakeProxy` has no `default:` label — an unknown type writes **nothing**, leaving the proxy as-is.\n- The inverted GJK cache-validity test `!(min < max*2 && metric < -1.0e8f)`, which makes the cache almost always accepted.\n- `c2Simplex` laid out as `[c2sv; 4]` so the C idiom `c2sv *verts = &s.a; verts[i]` works with the identical 152-byte layout.\n- Every array index that C leaves unchecked (`cache->iA[i]`, `pA.verts[iA]`, `saveA[i]`) uses raw pointer arithmetic, so a hostile cache reads adjacent memory as in C instead of panicking/aborting.\n- Comparison-vs-NaN branch polarity checked against GCC's `comiss`/`jbe` for every `<=`/`>` in `c22`, `c23`, `c2Maxv`, `c2Minv`, `c2GJK`.\n\n## Known unmatchable case (C undefined behaviour)\n\n`c2GJK` declares `c2Proxy pA, pB;` **uninitialized**. If a caller supplies a `c2GJKCache` whose `iA`/`iB` exceed the proxy's `count` (violating the cache contract), the C reads uninitialized stack whose content depends on the caller's frame residue. Rust zero-initializes, so results differ there. I isolated this precisely: restricting cache indices to in-range values makes 21.3 M checks pass, and 1.6 M realistic cache-reuse checks pass. No reachable in-contract input diverges.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `c_src/` is byte-for-byte untouched (mtimes unchanged, no build dir created inside it); I built the reference `.so` into a separate directory.\n- Scratch dirs `cbuild/`, `difftest/` and `*_syms.txt` remain at the top level — the sandbox denied my `rm -rf` cleanup. They sit outside both `c_src/` and `translation/` and don't affect either build."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":683,"cache_read_input_tokens":150804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":683,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4909f959-d064-4890-93b8-dfb278c3e047","uuid":"39492da9-cc08-443b-ad77-4515eaeac462","timestamp":"2026-08-27T06:44:53.486Z"}
